# URL parity for the Astro rebuild.
#
# This file mirrors the `[[redirects]]` rules in netlify.toml, because a site that
# is deployed WITHOUT a build step (branch deploy of the prebuilt output, or a
# direct draft deploy) reads _redirects and does not read netlify.toml. Both lists
# are identical; netlify.toml is the copy a built site uses.
#
# No real page URL changes in this migration — these only make the canonical form
# explicit and add short aliases that currently 404.

/index.html              /                        301
/pages/about.html        /pages/about             301
/pages/register.html     /pages/register          301
/pages/fields.html       /pages/fields            301
/pages/contact.html      /pages/contact           301
/pages/physical.html     /pages/physical          301
/pages/thankyou.html     /pages/thankyou          301

/about                   /pages/about             301
/register                /pages/register          301
/fields                  /pages/fields            301
/contact                 /pages/contact           301
/physical                /pages/physical          301
/thankyou                /pages/thankyou          301
